{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1000626-theory-supernal-is-\u2018ordered\u2019-abyss","id":1000626,"title":"[Theory] Supernal is \u2018ordered\u2019 Abyss","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-08T23:26:39-08:00","id":1000626,"title":"[Theory] Supernal is \u2018ordered\u2019 Abyss","content":"Watching lately Marvel\u2019s <b>Doctor Strange</b> and reading <b>Locke &amp; Key</b> comic series, I come to some brave theory...<br /> <br /> <b>What if Supernal Realms are coming from the same source as Abyss, only that they are \u2018ordered\u2019, when Void is force of pure chaos and impossibility?</b> That first mages ( or Atlantis ) harnessed chaotic energies of Abyss and chained them to stable Symbols running reality, limiting madness of sorcerers.<br /> <br /> If even this is not main gameline assumption, what changes would be needed to game to accommodate this point of view?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-09-2016, 02:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T23:47:51-08:00","id":1000632,"title":"","content":"One of my interpretations is, more or less, similar- the Abyss is everything the Supernal is not. That is, both are collection of symbols, and as such all come from the same &quot;origin&quot;- but where the Supernal mean things, the Abyss is defined by negativity. Every symbol which is not part of the Supernal (and as such, does not exist) is the &quot;Abyss&quot;, which means it can only be defined by not being the Supernal (because it does not exist). The first humans has defined the world around them, collecting the symbols of the world and by doing so created the Supernal- and by defining what &quot;is&quot;, they also created &quot;what isn't&quot;, and forced the Abyss- which previously didn't existed- into existence. It never forgave them for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T23:58:23-08:00","id":1000637,"title":"","content":"Is an interesting theory. The first mages, working with the raw chaos of creation to birth a source of more stable magic resonates well with lots of creation myths all over the world. I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T02:26:05-08:00","id":1000671,"title":"","content":"You don't have to change anything to accommodate that view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T02:54:03-08:00","id":1000681,"title":"","content":"It's the belief system of the Scelesti with less coherence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T03:59:43-08:00","id":1000695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1000626-theory-supernal-is-\u2018ordered\u2019-abyss?p=1000671#post1000671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't have to change anything to accommodate that view.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do not Paradox is 'eating' magic by RAW? In this theory-view, it should not, as magic is the same as Paradox - only Paradox is 'wild', why Supernal Magic is 'tamed'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-09-2016, 07:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T04:07:16-08:00","id":1000697,"title":"","content":"Paradox simply changes and corrupts cast spells. I think it's exactly what you're after. However, the piece of abyss in Sleepers that leads to Dissonance will unravel cast spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T04:43:10-08:00","id":1000702,"title":"","content":"This idea was already suggested in the Scelesti section of the Left Hand Path book. You don't have to change anything, since its already a theory in Awakening. Of course, its likely going to stay just a theory, because its impossible to go back in time to directly observe such an occurance, but if you add mage research that lends weight to the idea, much like we have weight behind the idea of the Big Bang, you're good to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T04:54:06-08:00","id":1000704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1000626-theory-supernal-is-\u2018ordered\u2019-abyss?p=1000695#post1000695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do not Paradox is 'eating' magic by RAW? In this theory-view, it should not, as magic is the same as Paradox - only Paradox is 'wild', why Supernal Magic is 'tamed'.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Paradox doesn't eat magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T06:16:41-08:00","id":1000734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1000626-theory-supernal-is-\u2018ordered\u2019-abyss?p=1000704#post1000704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Paradox doesn't eat magic.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Mage</b> 2E corebook seems to point other way around:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage 2E, p.115</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Casting the Spell</b><br /> Once all dice penalties and bonuses are calculated, including any penalties from Paradox, the player rolls dice. A single success on the casting means the spell effect takes place.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage 2E, p.116</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a single success is rolled on the Paradox dice, a Paradox occurs.<br /> The Abyss taints the spell and, potentially, the area around the spell\u2019s subject. The Paradox imposes a dice penalty to the spellcasting roll equal to its successes. Whether or not this makes the spell fail, a Paradox anomaly occurs. If the spellcasting results in a dramatic failure, the mage incurs a Paradox Condition as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Paradox successes can lower spellcasting roll to 0 dices, it's 'eating magic' in my book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T06:29:43-08:00","id":1000740,"title":"","content":"No, it's corrupting it. Corruption might involve weakening the effect, but it's not simple consumption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T06:36:19-08:00","id":1000745,"title":"","content":"If you summon Intruder with your spell, and cannot cast spell because of it, I say that Abyss 'kills/eats' Supernal. It also more obvious in Supernal Being Summoning:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage 2E, p. 96</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once the being runs out of Corpus, it vanishes. The denizens can sense when their time is running out, and usually attempt to get back into the summoning circle, so that they can go directly home.<br /> <br /> If, however, the creature \u201cdies\u201d outside of the summoning circle, or is killed by a deliberate magical attack, it cannot use the path laid down by the mage to reach its home again. <b>Instead, it vanishes into the Abyss. This is obvious to anyone watching \u2014 black tendrils may extend from the walls and rip it to shreds, or an Abyssal being might manifest to collect it. </b><br /> <br /> In any event, directly contributing to the death of a Supernal entity in this way is an Act of Hubris for Falling Wisdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T07:07:13-08:00","id":1000761,"title":"","content":"A Supernal being vanishing into the Abyss is not the same as saying it's been eaten which implies a cessation of existence.<br /> <br /> In fact, note the fact that it says the Supernal being &quot;dies&quot;, the quotation marks let you know that they in fact don't die, at least in the usual sense despite any similarities to death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T07:18:33-08:00","id":1000768,"title":"","content":"This and that are separate issues. Supernal creatures have to bridge over the Abyss before coming to reality in the first place. Dying outside of a safe path means that they fall instead of staying on the bridge when they're being &quot;banished&quot; forcefully. This is not the Abyss eating the Supernal so much as the Supernal beings &quot;falling&quot; into the Abyss like an angel falling from heaven to be corrupted into a demon. Creatures and spells are not the same thing at all.<br /> <br /> The section on paradox specifically talks about tainting and warping spells. The book talks about paradox and the Abyss making the spell fly out of control, which is it is opposed by Wisdom, the stat that represents control over magic. Then, there's the fact that Paradox can make spells <i>stronger</i> rather than weaker. Irregardless of your dice roll getting zero successes due to paradox, <i>magic still happens</i>. Its just wildly out of your control and doesn't do what you want. That's completely opposite to the idea of &quot;eating magic.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, but the book doesn't support that view at all. If you want to run things that way, more power to you, but its not something cannon. <br /> <br /> Now, individual Acamoth, Golmoth or Intruders might want to eat magic, but that is something unique to said individual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 11-09-2016, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T07:28:50-08:00","id":1000772,"title":"","content":"Besides, for realms that &quot;eat&quot; stuff we already have the Lower Depths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T09:28:52-08:00","id":1000840,"title":"","content":"Without the eating of magic it does stand to reason that, at some point, the 'Fallen World' was just another world in the Abyss that eventually decided the impossible thing it wanted to be was static.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T09:49:08-08:00","id":1000848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1000626-theory-supernal-is-\u2018ordered\u2019-abyss?p=1000840#post1000840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without the eating of magic it does stand to reason that, at some point, the 'Fallen World' was just another world in the Abyss that eventually decided the impossible thing it wanted to be was static.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the Fallen World was separate until the Fall, which might have introduced the influence of both the Abyss and Supernal. The Fallen reflects the Supernal <i>now</i>, and so Awakened assume that was always the case. And considering retroactive time manipulation is on the table, how much does that mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T12:54:19-08:00","id":1000945,"title":"","content":"I've actually made a Banisher Nameless Order based around the belief that the Supernal and Abyss are the same plane of existence, just viewed from different lenses. Their Order is sorta like the Logophages, where they try to erase all traces and knowledge of Supernal Magic because seeing how reality acts to it when compared to the Abyss hints at them being near identical. Mind you, this is purely their own beliefs but as Dark Eras has shown us the Atlantean Paradigm isn't as old and iron clad as the Diamond and Seers would like all Mages to believe. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}